 "_": [
  "Words a figure draws for itself — as curves, or as pixels inside a placed",
  "picture — rather than setting as text. Those cannot be swapped run by run",
  "like the rest, so each one names the box it occupies, in the figure's own",
  "units, and the English that replaces it. Everything the box covers is taken",
  "out and the new word set in its place.",
  "",
  "`build.py --outlines <id>` lists the boxes and baselines a figure's own",
  "words occupy; `size` is needed wherever a descender makes the box taller",
  "than the type, and `align: start` keeps a label that runs on (\"Period 1\",",
  "whose number is drawn separately) beginning where it began."
